  "question": {
    "text": "A force is applied to a steel wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, rigidly clamped at one end. As a result elongation in the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math>. If same force is applied to another steel wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;of double the length and a diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math> times that of the wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, the elongation in the wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;will be (wires having uniform circular cross sections)"
  },
